commit ffd76f1031c1ced868fc7740b8f4bd8e523fbfea
Author: Martin Oberzalek <martin.oberzalek@anton-paar.com>
Date:   Wed Sep 23 13:34:39 2026 +0200

    Phase 1 done: cpputilstest-style suite + vendored miniLZO
    
    Implements Phase 1 of PLAN_rfa_tools.md. make check now builds and runs
    src_test_rfa/test_rfa.exe: 21/21 testcases pass.
    
    New:
    * testcommon/ - TestUtils (TestCaseBase plus the four canned case types),
      ColBuilder (ASCII result table) and TestRunner, API-compatible with
      majorkingleo/cpputilstest. Upstream repeats the run/report loop in every
      test_<component>.cc; hoisting it into TestRunner makes each program a list.
    * src_test_rfa/ - test_rfa.cc runner, test_testcommon (harness self-tests, so a
      silently-passing harness cannot masquerade as green) and test_lzo (codec
      round-trip, 32 KiB chunk boundaries, truncated input, and the LZO1X
      literal-run encoding pinned against the Phase 0 experiment).
    * third_party/minilzo/ - miniLZO 2.10 vendored unmodified, with COPYING and a
      provenance README. Deliberately not under cpputils/, which is a submodule.
    * Makefile.am - check_PROGRAMS/TESTS wiring and the noinst libraries; plus a
      make check VS Code task.
    
    Fixed:
    * configure.ac, Makefile.am and reconfigure.sh were checked in with CRLF
      endings. The AC_CONFIG_FILES entry became "Makefile\r", so configure died
      with "cannot find input file", and the stray CR overwrote the error text in
      the terminal. reconfigure.sh also failed outright under Cygwin, meaning the
      reconfigure task added in Phase 0 never actually worked. Converted to LF and
      pinned with .gitattributes.
    * TestCaseFuncOneFile now deletes its scratch file after the run.
    * libminilzo needs a per-target CPPFLAGS: AM_CPPFLAGS carries -std=c++20, which
      is not valid for a C translation unit.
    
    The suite earned its keep immediately: it caught that sizing a decompression
    buffer from the compressed size is wrong (33-byte-repeating input compresses
    well over 64x, yielding LZO_E_OUTPUT_OVERRUN). The RFA reader must use the
    uncompressedSize from the directory table instead.

